WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.460
The battle royal determines the semfinal matchups.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:30.320
Yugi, it seems you want to duel the scrub, but I won't allow collusion.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.200
Our duel of destiny awaits in the semifinals.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.860
For that to happen, I must get rid of the scrub and Marik.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:43.110
The duel is reaching its climax!

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:49.120
Each Player's Opponent

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.210
My turn!

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.480
I summon Dark Jeroid!

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.450
It has an effect.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:26.530
When it's summoned, it can lower a monster's attack points by 800.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:37.150
Which monster shall I choose?

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.070
Attack me, Marik.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:43.010
I'll catch you in my trap.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:48.950
Ring of Destruction will greatly reduce your life points.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.200
A trap, huh?  How obvious.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.820
The Pharaoh's Archfiend of Gilfer has 2200 attack points.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:03.760
Even if Dark Jeroid lowers it by 800, it will still have 1400 attack points.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.480
It'll have 200 more points than Dark Jeroid.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.430
Then it's obvious.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.480
My target is Jonouchi's Gearfried!

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.070
I knew it!

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.150
Dark Jeroid's effect activates!

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.110
Gearfried loses 800 attack points!

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.880
Die!

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.440
Whatever!

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.630
Not gonna happen!

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:31.540
I activate my set card!

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.000
Skull Dice!

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.400
It'll lower your monster's attack points!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.330
You only rely on luck!

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.140
Be quiet!  Here I go!

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.220
I rolled a 2!

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:50.830
Your Dark Jeroid's attack points are halved!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.710
Good!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.100
Too bad, Marik.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.450
Your monster is counterattacked!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.450
Gearfried, Iron Chop!

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.690
What?

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.630
No way!  It shrank!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.540
What happened?

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.880
I activated my set card, Shrink!

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.540
This spell card cuts a monster's attack points in half.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:29.140
Jonouchi, your Gearfried's attack points drop to 500!

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.110
It's so tiny.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.280
Dark Jeroid, destroy Gearfried!

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.660
Dammit, Kaiba!

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.630
How dare you interfere!

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.060
Jonouchi.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.540
I knew Kaiba would try something.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:51.840
He's such a jerk.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.280
But it was a strategic move.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.510
Still...

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:59.000
Kaiba still has two set cards.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.440
They have to be careful.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.220
Impressive, big brother!

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.120
His activation timing was perfect!

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.900
Listen up!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.550
All my opponents can be useful.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.920
For me to win.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.980
Say what!

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.890
Jonouchi, stay calm.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.600
You'll get a chance to win.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.340
Here I go!  My turn!

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.470
Mai.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.030
Mai!

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.420
Who was that?

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.680
I don't know.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:48.440
I know my brother will save you.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.060
I'll stay with Mai.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:57.430
So focus on the duel and win, Brother!

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.170
My turn!

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:00.620
I draw!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.810
How are the other players doing this turn?

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:11.020
Kaiba has two set cards and Blade Knight in attack position.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:17.460
Marik has no set cards and Dark Jeroid in attack position.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:25.150
And Jonouchi has one set card only.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.520
He's in bad shape.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:30.370
Hey!  Stop looking at me like that!

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.070
I know my field is empty!

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:39.200
Of all monsters on the field, my Archfiend of Gilfer has the most attack points.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.260
But I'm worried about Kaiba's two set cards.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.900
They're probably traps.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.030
I can't attack him carelessly.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.900
Who should I attack?

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:52.220
Well then...

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.490
You're my target!

00:06:54.700 --> 00:07:00.500
Yugi cares about his promise with Jonouchi.  To battle as true duelists.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.930
So he's only targeting Marik and Kaiba.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.770
But look at Jonouchi.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:13.260
Jonouchi's anger is directed towards Marik.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.550
Yeah.  Jonouchi wants Marik.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:20.980
He personally wants to save Mai from Marik.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:29.730
Dammit!

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.660
I promise to save Mai.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.660
With my own hands!

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:36.920
Jonouchi...

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.970
As a duelist...

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.270
...and as a friend who fought by my side, I want to save her.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:49.080
Because she's always been saving me.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.160
You're right.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.380
Hey!  What do you mean, "you're right?"

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.380
Anzu, don't tell Yugi.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:56.820
Why not?

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:05.100
We promised that we'd fight fair and square as true duelists.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.760
True duelists?

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:11.200
I don't know if I qualify yet.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.530
But I know this:

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:17.640
If I can't save Mai, I'm not a true duelist.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.300
Brother...

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:29.880
In order to fulfill my promise with Yugi, I must defeat Marik and save Mai.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.280
I see...

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.120
He said that?

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:37.060
It's rather like him.

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:42.710
He blames himself for failing to protect Mai.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:45.460
Archfiend of Gilfer attacks!

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.350
The target monster is...

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:48.770
Yugi!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.370
Time out!

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:53.260
Umm, Yugi...

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.150
What's a true duelist?

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.580
Jonouchi?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.570
Archfiend of Gilfer attacks!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.430
The target monster is...

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.700
Yugi!  Time out!

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:24.140
Umm, Yugi...

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.740
What's a true duelist?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.410
Jonouchi?

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:32.180
What's he suddenly talking about?

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:34.350
One thing is clear.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:39.140
A true duelist wouldn't call a time out during someone else's turn.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.290
True.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:45.730
I've come this far in Battle City searching for that answer.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:51.900
So that I can fight you fair and square, Yugi.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:59.160
By dueling many people in the city, I think I'm finding the answer little by little.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.140
What a pathetically bland journey.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:08.300
Yugi, you taught me to face my opponents without fear.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:13.090
To never give up and believe in my cards.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:14.640
Honda!

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.520
W-What's up?

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.860
You taught me to trust each other, even in difficult times.

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:23.060
Why's he saying this now?

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.800
He's creeping me out.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:29.220
And to all the duelists I fought...

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.410
Stop!

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:47.760
I win this duel!

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.190
Long time no see, Jonouchi.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.860
There you are, Insector Haga!

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:56.840
I was looking forward to meeting you again.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:09.080
Attack, my Queen!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.920
Queen's Hell Breath!

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.750
Haga, the duel is already over.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:17.890
What?

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:21.420
I activate the trap card, Graverobber!

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.130
Graverobber?

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.200
Yeah.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.060
The card I'm taking from your graveyard is...

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.900
I really don't like bugs.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.010
Yeah!  Insect Queen is destroyed!

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.450
Fortress Whale is sunk!

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.040
I play the spell card, Return of the Doomed.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.160
It resurrects the monster that was destroyed this turn.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:05.780
What's up?  Come at me!

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:10.580
You talk a big game, so show me how you fight!

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:14.200
I can't afford to lose either.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:17.560
There's a battle that I want to fight.

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.680
I won't give up!

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.480
I activate a spell card!

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:25.360
Giant Trunade!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:33.830
What?

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:38.360
I'm not willing to leave this card in the graveyard.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:41.840
I have no regrets!

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:43.270
Bring it, Jonouchi!

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:49.180
Thanks to them, I found my shortcomings that I was unaware of.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.850
I've grown as a duelist.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:04.500
Mai!  They haven't picked your opponent yet.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:08.430
I'm going to win, no matter who I face.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:12.400
Yugi and Jonouchi, I'll see you in the semifinals!

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:13.960
Jonouchi!

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:19.900
I'm not a spoiled duelist like you who can't duel unless people cheer for you!

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.600
You're right, Mai.

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:28.780
You also taught me many important things.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:33.280
Only one can gain the glory in Battle City!

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:36.930
Everyone is your enemy in a battle royal!

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.330
You're making me yawn.

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.710
Continue the duel already!

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:50.700
Yugi!  If you're a true duelist, then fight me like an opponent!

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.940
Stop protecting me just because you want to fulfill our promise!

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:56.310
Jonouchi....

00:13:56.620 --> 00:14:02.650
Since I only have one set card, it's obvious that I'm in the worst situation.

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:04.180
Jonouchi...

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:07.820
Jonouchi has the most life points, but...

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:14.960
A single direct attack from Archfiend of Gilfer will put him at the top.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:19.830
Defeat the one closest to defeat!  That's how dueling works, Yugi!

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:23.440
Attack me without mercy during your turn!

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:24.600
Jonouchi...

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:31.000
Even if I lose here, I'll win the semifinals and duel you in the finals!

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:34.330
If you trust me, attack me!

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:35.330
Yugi!

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.120
Jonouchi, this is your card.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:47.060
Yugi, I can't take that Red-Eyes right now.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:52.000
Jonouchi, I'll wait for you.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.760
I'll hold on to your Red-Eyes until then.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.410
I understand, Jonouchi.

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:03.680
Let's duel in the finals!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.560
Archfiend of Gilfer attacks!

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:09.780
Attack Jonouchi directly!

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.050
Gilfer Flame!

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:19.830
Jonouchi...

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.040
Get ready, Marik.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:35.840
I'm taking you down with me.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.990
Mai, I promise to save you.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:47.640
Jonouchi!

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.490
Jonouchi only has a few life points left.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.840
My turn!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:54.860
I draw!

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:03.580
Mai, why are you doing this for me?

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.740
You don't have time to waste!

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:07.910
Win, Jonouchi.

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:09.240
Yeah.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:14.600
A single tear for your sister may someday become a bright light.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:20.350
Mai, I promise to retrieve your light.

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:22.270
I summon Axe Raider!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.760
Is he going to attack Marik?  Or...

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.430
I'm attacking...

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:38.070
You, Kaiba!

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:40.800
Kaiba?

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.400
Not Marik?

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.670
What's he thinking?

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.810
I thought he wanted to save Mai.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.810
Why did he change his target?

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:53.990
Was he pretending to attack Marik when he wanted to attack Kaiba instead?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:57.480
I knew Jonouchi was a loser.

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:00.930
He can't beat my brother!  He's going to self-destruct!

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.160
Here I go!

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.700
Axe Raider attacks Blade Knight!

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.680
Bring it, scrub!

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:08.740
Kaiba has set a trap.

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:09.870
I know.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.970
Take this!  Gale Slice!

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.680
I activate my trap card!

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.980
Ring of Destruction!

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.580
Ring of Destruction?

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:28.190
The equipped monster is destroyed, and both players take damage equal to its attack points.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.500
But I don't intend to die with that scrub!

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:34.820
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Ring of Defense!

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:38.600
I take no damage from a trap!

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:47.340
Jonouchi!  It's game over for you!

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:52.300
Jonouchi!

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.780
Jonouchi will have 0 life points?

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:58.570
As expected, Jonouchi is the first to lose.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:17:59.220
No.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.920
You're wrong.

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:06.090
I have 0 life points?

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:08.530
What happened?

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.630
I activated Graverobber.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:20.410
Graverobber steals a card from my opponent's graveyard.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:28.780
Marik, I used it to take Spell of Pain from your graveyard.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:35.890
This card let me transfer the damage I took to all the other players.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.000
Nice, Jonouchi!

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.690
It's just like you to benefit at someone's expense!

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.360
Way to go, Jonouchi!

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:45.130
Yeah!

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:47.580
Good thinking, Jonouchi.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:54.520
If Axe Raider attacked Dark Jeroid, Marik would've only taken 500 points of damage.

00:18:54.740 --> 00:19:01.680
So he attacked Kaiba instead, expecting that he'd use a trap that would trigger Graverobber...

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:06.120
...activating Spell of Pain to finish Marik.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:09.120
Excellent strategy, Jonouchi!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.560
See ya!

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:18.240
You'll regret this.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:25.170
The first player in the semifinals is Marik.

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:27.110
And I'll be next.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:32.880
But Jonouchi now doesn't have any monsters or set cards.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:36.820
So how can he deal with my brother's next attack?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:37.650
Quiet you!

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:41.020
Yup.  My field is empty.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.320
Exactly as I planned.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.260
I end my turn.

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:49.110
Exactly as you planned?

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:50.670
Don't make me laugh!

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:53.000
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:57.400
Since you rely on luck, you never had a plan!

00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:01.360
Blade Knight!  Attack Jonouchi directly!

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:05.380
Vanish, Jonouchi!

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.020
Jonouchi!

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.950
Let's meet in the finals, Yugi!

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.090
This is fine.

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:22.490
The battle royal was only for deciding the semifinal matchups.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.500
Thanks for waiting.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:29.020
You're going to the shadows.

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:33.340
You're the one who's gonna lose, Marik!

